WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.769
-Wow! Everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.570
-How does it feel? Tell me.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.373
-We made it through the rain.

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.809
We're back! We're back!

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.178
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.846
Alright. And guess what?

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.915
I was about to come out.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.550
I just found these sunglasses.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.319
I've been looking for them
for over a year,

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.722
which was the last time
I wore this freaking suit.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.190
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.
-No joke.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.692
-How ridiculous. Oh, my.
How are you feeling right now?

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.461
What did that just feel like?
-I feel great.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.030
First of all...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.667
...I understand
that this is only 58 people.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.270
It is still more than double
the size of my normal audience.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.639
-Yeah.
-This is certainly

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.041
the most people
I've seen in over a year.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.309
-Yeah.
-This is great.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.510
Your energy is awesome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.179
It's so cool
to be back at 30 Rock.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.348
Great to see you.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.150
-I got to talk to you
about the Clubhouse.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.186
I want to talk about
the docuseries.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.487
I want to talk about this.
-Yes.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.589
-I'm so into this,
I can't even tell you.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.691
You know me. I love reality TV.
-Thank you. I know you do.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.361
-Can you believe this?
I'm doing research on you.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.530
You've been on TV for
almost a decade? Over a decade.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.432
-I've been on
over a decade, yeah.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.900
About 15 years, I think.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.136
"Watch What Happens: Live"
has been on 12 years.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.005
-That's -- 12 years?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.139
Yeah.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.141
-You're amazing.
-You've been on 12 years --

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.343
You've been hosting "Late Night"
for 12 years.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.511
-Yeah.
-On NBC.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.180
-Yeah, you're right.
Kind of started together.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.213
-Yeah.
-That's wild.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.615
-Yeah.
-I love you, and I --

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.916
Dude, the shows are
still phenomenal.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:27.453
Even though you're doing it
during this pandemic,

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.455
the quarantine,
you're doing it all great.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.957
And baby steps.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.425
-Yeah. I can't wait
until we get an audience.

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.061
I mean, I'm just waiting.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.964
-Oh, wait till you --
Wait till you get it.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:41.768
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.470
But this --

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.372
I want to talk about this,
'cause this Thursday,

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.408
you have a new limited series

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.210
about the history
and impact of reality TV.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.244
It's on E!

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:55.147
Set your DVRs,
9:00, this Thursday.

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.282
You know I'm the biggest fan.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.617
So talk to me. What was --

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.120
-We go inside "The Bachelor,"
"The Kardashians,"

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.957
the "Housewives," "The Swan" --
Remember "The Swan"?

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:06.125
-Oh, my God.
-I interview a few contestants

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:08.427
from "The Swan"
and see how it all held up.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:11.230
-Wait, wait. "The Swan,"
if I can remember well,

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.232
Was it someone
who did plastic surgery?

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.267
-It's kind of a plastic surgery
beauty pageant.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.469
-Oh.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.638
-You know, lot of great
ideas in reality TV.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.639
Lot of maybe not-so-great ideas.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.909
-Do you remember when I loved,
and it was everyone --

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.311
Obviously, you can't do it,
and you shouldn't have done it.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.379
-Right. What?

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.580
-"Kid Nation,"
do you remember that?

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.916
-"Kid Nation,"
we cover, absolutely.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.517
A horrible idea.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:35.221
Kids! It was basically
a reality "Lord of the Flies."

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.255
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.757
-Like, who let their kids
go do that show?

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:39.859
-Dude, they ran the town.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.594
-Oh, we definitely
talk about "Kid Nation."

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.896
We talk to some of
the former kids from the show.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.097
-No!

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:46.566
-Yes, we do.
-No.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.434
-We do. And we talk
to Molly and Jason

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.236
who fell in love
on "The Bachelor,"

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.739
and they really
sang like canaries

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:57.877
about producer involvement
and enhancement on that show.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.813
I found it very interesting
and surprising.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.081
-Really?
-Yes.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.515
-And this other thing
that you talk about,

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:06.085
that I want to talk about
tonight, because this was odd.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.420
I was talking to you backstage.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.922
I said, you talked
to Khloé Kardashian,

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.991
and you said,
"I'm pronouncing her name --

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.493
We've all been pronouncing her
name wrong this whole time."

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.996
-It's "Klo-ay."
Khloé is the name.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.331
There is a little accent
over the name.

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:21.467
And so, I went and interviewed
the Kardashians

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.035
at Khloé's house.

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:24.737
-Wait, wait. I'm so sorry.
No, no. I'm sorry.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:25.938
-Yes.
-No, no, no, no.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:27.406
-Sorry, sorry, but --

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.875
-Yeah, I'm sorry, too, but --
-Call her. Call her.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.011
-I will call her Khloé.
-I walked in, I go, "Khloé"

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.780
and the other women go,
"Excuse me?"

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.382
And Chris said, "Yeah,

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.719
that's actually really
how it's pronounced."

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.086
-'Cause there is a little --

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:43.022
-There is a little thing
on top of the name.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.891
Why am I the only one
that got that?

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.792
-Khloé?
-I got the memo.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.327
-Khloé.
-Yes.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:49.962
-Wow.
-Ask her.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:51.630
-Wow! Khloé.
-Yes.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.000
-It was wild. It was a trip
going to the Kardashians' house.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.803
You got to go through
all these gates.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:59.071
I had to get a COVID test
before I got there.

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.940
-Wait, like "Get Smart"?

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.241
-Kind of like "Get Smart."

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:03.575
And they were like, I said,

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:05.644
"Oh, you want to give me
the results of the COVID test?"

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.980
They go, "Go to Khloé's,

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.216
and if the second gate opens,

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.350
you're negative."
-Go to Khlo-B's.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.386
Go to Khlo-B's.
-Yes. Go Khlo-B's.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.920
And the gate opened. I was like,

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.656
"Alright, I don't have COVID.
I'm good."

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.990
-So you made it
through the second gate.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.025
-I did, straight to the --
-And there's a third gate?

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:23.229
-There are so many gates,
I don't even remember, honestly.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:25.898
-And what were they like?
-They were amazing.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.901
The lighting setup
is very intense.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.236
They looked so beautiful.
-They do.

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:33.372
-And they're all kind of
casually hanging out

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:36.242
on these swings
behind Khloé's house.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.843
It was wild.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:39.845
-I want to show everyone a clip
from the series.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:41.881
Here's Andy Cohen
with the Kardashians

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.950
in "For Real:
The Story of Reality TV."

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.152
Take a look at this.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.154
-What do you think
the legacy of the show is?

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.755
-Just family over everything.

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:52.191
I think at the start
of this show,

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:55.728
our first meeting was that
we just wanted to make sure

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:58.331
that our heart came through

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:01.500
and we didn't really leave
every episode with drama,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.503
that it was back to the family,
back at heart.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:07.106
-Well said. It's just
how we live our lives.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.340
-Right.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.742
-And we spend so much time
together off-camera.

00:05:10.742 --> 00:05:12.145
Like, two nights ago,

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:15.248
we all ended up randomly
at Kim's house.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:18.951
She had this chiropractor over,
and I was fixing something

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.419
and somebody else would walk in

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.887
and, you know.
-Rob was there.

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.457
-We had like three appointments
going on, like, in a circle.

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.624
Like, "Who wants a spray tan,

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.392
then the chiropractor,
then a facial?"

00:05:27.392 --> 00:05:31.531
-Okay, that's the scenario
that I envision happening.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:34.433
-[ Laughing ] Yeah,
that's exactly what --

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:35.734
-Who wants a spray tan?

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.670
-I cannot wait for this.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.238
How many parts is this?

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.439
-Seven.
-Seven parts.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.174
-Seven parts.
We cover every show.

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.375
-"Real World," MTV?

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:46.145
-Yes. I cried.
I reunited the original cast.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.247
I cried when they came out.
I died.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.581
-Wait, Eric?

00:05:49.581 --> 00:05:51.650
-Eric.
-Heather B?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.487
-Yeah, my girl Heather B, yes.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:55.621
-Wow, I can't wait for this.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.756
Andy and I are going
to go head-to-head

00:05:57.756 --> 00:06:00.659
in "One-Second Reality TV Quiz"
when we come back.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:01.694
Stick around, everybody.

